+# Positioning update — 1 October 2026
+
+This note is outside the frozen dataset v1.1.2. It adds no historical event and changes no mathematical label in the CSVs.
+
+## Public corpus boundary
+
+The public pilot has 21 events, 13 sources and 7 claim identifiers across four cases. The source register contains 3 public originals, 9 private/internal originals and 1 private original; non-public originals are not redistributed. The corpus is partly reconstructed retrospectively. It is neither a complete interaction transcript nor a representative benchmark of model reliability.
+
+## Literature comparisons
+
+PROV-O, micropublications and nanopublications are established antecedents. PRM800K and ProcessBench already represent mathematical errors; no priority for preserving negative data is claimed. Additional comparisons include Evidence-Ledger (arXiv:2607.26512v1), TheoremGraph (arXiv:2606.25363v1), the authors’ PreprintPaperTracker repository and the conceptual, non-peer-reviewed Reinforcement Learning Contour v1. These have different units and goals; their relevance is not a claim that their datasets are identical to this pilot.
+
+- https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/
+- https://doi.org/10.1186/2041-1480-5-28
+- https://nanopub.net/guidelines/working_draft/
+- https://github.com/openai/prm800k
+- https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.06559
+- https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.26512v1
+- https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.25363v1
+- https://github.com/rustlab1/PreprintPaperTracker
+- https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202608.0212/v1
+
+## Truth and novelty
+
+Reclassification as classical does not make a true theorem REFUTED. Truth/warrant, novelty, diffusion and documentary condition are separate questions. The frozen schema has four state axes and does not yet include a dedicated novelty axis. A schema extension must be versioned explicitly.
+
+## HOL2 as later context
+
+For odd primes p, reduction SL₂(Z/p^(n+1)Z) → SL₂(Z/p^nZ) splits only when (p,n)=(3,1). The first-level obstruction for p≥5 is already given by Stasinski, §6, Theorem 6.2; that section refers to Sah for the classical classification. No general novelty is claimed. This contextual note does not establish when every claim was first made and does not add a retrospective event to the frozen corpus.
+
+Reference: A. Stasinski, Representations of SL_n over finite local rings of length two, Journal of Algebra 566 (2021), 119–135. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2020.08.036 ; https://arxiv.org/pdf/1907.09878
+
+The separate p=7 HOL-01 package retains its own scope. This repository does not bundle the full HOL2 mathematical replay, Barning–Hall certificates or a Lean verification of the corpus. A proposed Data Paper describes the existing pilot and is not represented as submitted or accepted.
